{"eligibility":"include","exclusion_criterion":"","side_list":"none","eligibility_reason":"Evaluates post-training weight quantization (six PTQ methods) applied to code LLMs. It measures NF quality of the generated code (SonarCloud maintainability, reliability, security, complexity) alongside pass@1. Borderline because quantization does not aim to improve NF quality.","title":"Quantize with Confidence? An Empirical Study of Quantization for Code Generation","year":2026,"venue":"preprint","venue_type":"preprint","study_type":"technique-evaluation","techniques":[{"technique_name":"4-bit post-training weight quantization (GPTQ, AWQ, QuIP#, AQLM, BitsAndBytes NF4, GGUF Q4_K_M)","family_v0":"other","stage":"training-time","signal_source":["none"],"tools":"SonarCloud; Lizard (qualitative example); WikiText-2 calibration for AQLM/QuIP#","iterations":"","dims_targeted":[],"dims_measured":["readability-maintainability","security"],"correctness_measured":true,"metrics":"maintainability: SonarCloud code smells, cyclomatic complexity, cognitive complexity, LoC [tool-static]; reliability: SonarCloud bugs [tool-static]; security: SonarCloud hotspots/vulnerabilities [tool-static]; correctness: pass@1","benchmarks":"McEval (Python 42, Java 53 tasks); CoderEval filtered (190 Python, 184 Java); BigCodeBench (Python)","languages":"Python, Java","models":"Qwen2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct, open, code-specialized instruct; CodeLlama-7B-Instruct, open, code-specialized instruct","baselines":"FP16 full-precision model","effect_target":"mixed","effect_target_headline":"AWQ again inflates Maintainability (328 vs. 273) — Qwen McEval-Java; d = −0.394, medium","effect_correctness":"mixed","effect_correctness_headline":"AQLM (p < 0.05, OR = 0.62) significantly improves it; QuIP# drops to 0.12 vs FP 0.23 on BCB-Python CodeLlama","effect_other_dims":{"readability-maintainability":"mixed","efficiency":"NR","security":"0"}}],"compute_reported":["time"],"contamination_handled":"no","human_eval":"none","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"https://github.com/empirical-quant-project/empirical-quantization-study","reimplementable":"yes","qa":{"QA1":1,"QA2":1,"QA3":1,"QA4":1,"QA5":1,"QA6":1,"QA7":0.5,"QA8":1,"QA9":0,"QA10":1},"confidence":"low","notes":"Borderline eligibility. Quantization is a weight-level intervention but is not intended to improve NF quality; reviewers may prefer to classify this as context. Tables are garbled: in particular, the column alignment of the Security and Reliability values is unclear. Most quality differences are non-significant. VRAM and throughput figures refer to model inference, not code efficiency."}
