{"eligibility":"exclude","exclusion_criterion":"IC3","side_list":"none","eligibility_reason":"The paper proposes a steering technique (MRepE) intended to improve readability, but it never measures the readability of code the LLM actually generates. Outcomes are the probability of yes/no answers to readability-judgment queries, NLL ratios of fixed readable vs unreadable code snippets, and multiple-choice correctness judgments.","title":"Towards the Readability of LLM-Generated Codes through Multitask Representation Engineering","year":2026,"venue":"preprint","venue_type":"","study_type":"","techniques":"","compute_reported":"","contamination_handled":"","human_eval":"","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"","qa":"","confidence":"medium","notes":"Borderline case. The technique is activation steering, an in-decoding intervention targeting readability (comment density, naming, cyclomatic complexity). However, all evaluation uses proxies: the model's judgment probabilities and the likelihood of pre-written MBPP-CR snippets. No generated code is scored with static tools or by humans. Correctness is likewise measured as multiple-choice accuracy on MBPP-CC. Figures are garbled in the extracted text. A reviewer should confirm that no generated-code readability metric appears in the appendix."}
