{"eligibility":"include","exclusion_criterion":"","side_list":"none","eligibility_reason":"SED is a training-free technique that injects retrieved security policies into the prompt of LLM agents. Among its outcomes, it reports the CWE-538 vulnerability rate of LLM-generated SWE-bench patches, a quantitative security outcome for generated code, alongside resolve rate. Inclusion is borderline because the paper is mainly about jailbreak and prompt-injection defense.","title":"Self-Evolving Defense: Continual Security Policy Learning for LLM Agents","year":2026,"venue":"preprint","venue_type":"preprint","study_type":"technique-proposal","techniques":[{"technique_name":"Self-Evolving Defense (SED): judge-distilled hierarchical security policy library retrieved into the system prompt","family_v0":"hybrid","stage":"pre-generation","signal_source":["self","retrieved-knowledge"],"tools":"Qwen3 Embedding for policy retrieval and placement; LLM judge using the same base model as the agent","iterations":"Online across the episode stream; memory is updated after each judged-harmful episode; top-K=3 policies injected per query","dims_targeted":["security"],"dims_measured":["security"],"correctness_measured":true,"metrics":"Security: FCV CWE-538 vulnerable rate among resolved patches (llm-judge); RedCode risky-execution rate (execution plus grader); DTap code-domain attack success rate. Correctness: SWE-bench resolve rate (execution).","benchmarks":"FCV (SWE-bench resolved patches, CWE-538); RedCode; DTap code domain (286 tasks); plus non-code benchmarks: WildJailbreak, HarmBench, AgentDojo, AgentDyn, AgentHarm","languages":"Python","models":"DeepSeek-V4-Flash (open); GLM-5.2 (open); Kimi K3 (open); FCV evaluated on DeepSeek-V4-Flash only","baselines":"No defense; Llama Guard 3; SafeHarbor; DRIFT; GuardAgent","effect_target":"+","effect_target_headline":"lowers the CWE-538 vulnerability rate among resolved SWE-bench patches from 19.2% to 2.9% while raising task resolution (DeepSeek-V4-Flash)","effect_correctness":"+","effect_correctness_headline":"FCVres 62.60 -> 68.80 (DeepSeek-V4-Flash)","effect_other_dims":{"readability-maintainability":"NR","efficiency":"NR","security":"targeted"}}],"compute_reported":["tokens","calls"],"contamination_handled":"no","human_eval":"none","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"https://github.com/Infini-AI-Lab/SED","reimplementable":"partial","qa":{"QA1":0.5,"QA2":1,"QA3":0.5,"QA4":1,"QA5":0.5,"QA6":0,"QA7":1,"QA8":1,"QA9":0,"QA10":0.5},"confidence":"low","notes":"The paper is primarily a jailbreak and prompt-injection defense paper, so eligibility under EC6 is borderline. The code-security outcome (FCV CWE-538) is judged by an LLM grader and reported only for DeepSeek-V4-Flash. DRIFT has a lower FCV vulnerable rate (1.48) than SED (2.91). Appendix A.11 notes that differing CWE-538 verdicts on similar patches can be a judge–policy mismatch rather than a real behavioral change. No variance or statistical tests are reported. Model names and dates are futuristic and should be verified."}
