{"eligibility":"include","exclusion_criterion":"","side_list":"none","eligibility_reason":"Proposes a multi-agent, verifier-guided pipeline that translates, repairs and compiles LLM-generated or LLM-edited code. It reports quantitative security outcomes on the final code: NVIDIA Compute Sanitizer memcheck/racecheck, SecCodePLT security tests, and robotics collision/out-of-bounds checks.","title":"MAGS: Multi-agent Auto-formalization Guarantees Safety for Agentic Outputs","year":2026,"venue":"preprint","venue_type":"preprint","study_type":"technique-proposal","techniques":[{"technique_name":"MAGS (multi-agent auto-formalization with Dafny verifier-guided repair and compile-back)","family_v0":"multi-agent","stage":"post-generation-loop","signal_source":["static-analyzer","other-LLM","human"],"tools":"Dafny (Boogie, Z3 SMT solver); Dafny compiler; NVIDIA Compute Sanitizer (evaluation only)","iterations":"retry budget of 25 total agent calls; 8 solver seeds; 500 s timeout per attempt; stops when Dafny verifies","dims_targeted":["security"],"dims_measured":["security"],"correctness_measured":true,"metrics":"security: verification success rate (formal verifier, tool-static); independent safety-check success: Compute Sanitizer memcheck/racecheck (execution), SecCodePLT security tests (execution), MuJoCo collision/out-of-bounds (execution). Correctness: functional preservation on 10 held-out LLM-generated tests (execution).","benchmarks":"KernelBench Level 1 (100); SecCodePLT sample (100, 27 CWEs); VLABench arm-control (20)","languages":"CUDA; Python; Dafny (intermediate representation)","models":"Opus 5 (closed); GPT 5.6 Sol (closed); Gemini 3.0 Thinking (closed, program source); Claude Fable 5.1 (closed, test generation)","baselines":"none (original program used only for the functional preservation comparison)","effect_target":"NR","effect_target_headline":"Safety check success: CUDA 100/100, Terminal 82/100, Robotics 20/20","effect_correctness":"mixed","effect_correctness_headline":"Functional preservation: CUDA 100/100, Terminal 100/100, Robotics 11/20","effect_other_dims":{"readability-maintainability":"NR","efficiency":"NR","security":"targeted"}}],"compute_reported":["tokens","cost","time"],"contamination_handled":"no","human_eval":"none","human_eval_details":"","artifact_url":"","reimplementable":"partial","qa":{"QA1":0.5,"QA2":0,"QA3":1,"QA4":1,"QA5":0.5,"QA6":0,"QA7":1,"QA8":0,"QA9":0,"QA10":0.5},"confidence":"medium","notes":"Model names (Opus 5, GPT 5.6 Sol, Claude Fable 5.1) and the 2026 dates look unusual; verify the paper's authenticity. There is no baseline safety rate for the original unverified programs, so the improvement direction cannot be established. Terminal programs come from the benchmark and may be human-written; the CUDA and robotics programs are generated by Gemini. A different model is used per domain."}
